<section class="process spacing">
    <h1>Process</h1>
    <ul id="gallery">
        <li id="process1/1">
            <img src="img/locupprocess1.png" alt="">
            <p>At the beginning of this project, I 
                had extravagant ideas of making the 
                box a dreadlock or boxes with intricate 
                functions, however, I simplified my 
                box to 1.) make a less expensive and 
                easier box to create and 2.) make the 
                experience of the user more streamlined 
                and intuitive.  </p>
        </li>
        <li id="process1/2">
            <img src="img/locupprocess2.png" alt="">
            <p>As I began coming up with names and the 
                look and feel of the brand, I reflected 
                on my own experience and how my experience 
                looking for hair care was. I decided to 
                use my own dreadlocks as a basis for the 
                logo and motifs to make them more personal 
                and unique. I also kept it a bit simple 
                with the name loc-up because most other 
                dreadlock brands will have overly thought names. </p>
        </li>
        <li id="process1/3">
            <img src="img/locupprocess3.png" alt="">
            <p>After drawing the dreadlock motifs I 
                tried to create the logo by completely 
                hand drawing the whole thing. I enjoyed 
                the look but it was starting to feel a 
                little unprofessional which was not the 
                look I was going for. </p>
        </li>
    </ul>
    <ul class="buttons">
        <a href="#process1/1"></a>
    <a href="#process1/2"></a>
    <a href="#process1/3"></a>
    </ul>
</section>